---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

// NOTE ON SCOPE (read before editing):
// This page pitches a referral partnership to treating physicians. It must not
// promise any product that does not exist. There is deliberately no mention of
// a doctor-facing dashboard, portal or adherence view - the Guide-facing view
// is not built. Everything offered here is delivered by hand, by email, today.
// If that changes, update this page then - not before.
const WA = 'https://wa.me/918359011231?text=Hi%20Akash%2C%20I%27m%20a%20doctor%20and%20I%27d%20like%20to%20talk%20about%20referrals.';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Sankalp for Doctors — Refer the Lifestyle Side, Keep the Clinical Side"
  description="You treat the condition. Sankalp works on what caused it — nutrition, sleep, movement, gut and emotional health — under your clinical ownership. No medication advice, ever. Referral partnership for physicians treating lifestyle conditions."
  path="/for-doctors.html"
  active="for-doctors"
>

<div class="scroll-bar" id="scrollBar"></div>

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="fd-hero" id="hero">
  <div class="fd-hero-fx" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="fd-hero-inner">
    <div class="kicker c">For Doctors</div>
    <h1 class="h1">You treat the condition.<br><em>Who's working on what caused it?</em></h1>
    <p class="lead c">Your prediabetic patient needs to change how they eat, sleep, move and handle stress. You have fifteen minutes and a full waiting room. I have the time you don't &mdash; and I don't go anywhere near your clinical decisions.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a href="#how" class="btn btn-primary">How referrals work &rarr;</a>
      <a href="#scope" class="btn btn-ghost">What I never touch</a>
    </div>

    <!-- the gap, visualised -->
    <div class="gapstrip reveal">
      <div class="gap-end">
        <div class="gap-num">15 min</div>
        <div class="gap-lbl">With you</div>
      </div>
      <div class="gap-mid"><span>the other 8,760 hours a year &mdash; where the condition is made or unmade</span></div>
      <div class="gap-end">
        <div class="gap-num">3 months</div>
        <div class="gap-lbl">Until review</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- PROBLEM -->
<section class="fd-section problem" id="problem">
  <div class="wrap narrow center">
    <div class="kicker c">The gap</div>
    <h2 class="h2">Advice isn't the missing piece.<br><em>Implementation is.</em></h2>
    <p class="lead c">Nobody reading this needs to be told that lifestyle drives metabolic disease. The problem was never the knowledge, or the prescription. It's that "lose weight, eat better, sleep more, reduce stress" is a destination handed to someone with no map, no route, and nobody walking alongside them.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chain">
      <div class="chain-step reveal">
        <div class="chain-dot"><div class="chain-num">1</div><div class="chain-line"></div></div>
        <div><h4>You diagnose accurately and prescribe appropriately</h4><p>The clinical decision is sound. Nothing on this page suggests otherwise.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="chain-step reveal">
        <div class="chain-dot"><div class="chain-num">2</div><div class="chain-line"></div></div>
        <div><h4>You add the lifestyle advice, in the time available</h4><p>Cut the sugar, walk daily, sleep earlier, manage the stress. All correct. All unactionable at that level of detail.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="chain-step reveal">
        <div class="chain-dot"><div class="chain-num">3</div><div class="chain-line"></div></div>
        <div><h4>They mean to. Then Monday happens</h4><p>They don't know what to eat at 9pm after a twelve-hour day, or which of the six things to start with. So they start none of them.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="chain-step reveal">
        <div class="chain-dot"><div class="chain-num">4</div><div class="chain-line"></div></div>
        <div><h4>Six months on, the numbers haven't moved</h4><p>Or they've drifted the wrong way. The dose goes up, and the conversation repeats.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="chain-step fail reveal">
        <div class="chain-dot"><div class="chain-num">5</div><div class="chain-line"></div></div>
        <div><h4>It gets recorded as non-compliance</h4><p>Occasionally that's what it is. Far more often, it's simply that nobody had the hours to show them how.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="punch reveal">That's the part I'd like to take off your hands.<br>None of the rest of it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHAT I WORK ON -->
<section class="fd-section" id="pillars">
  <div class="wrap narrow center">
    <div class="kicker c">What I work on</div>
    <h2 class="h2">Five pillars &mdash; <em>and nothing outside them.</em></h2>
    <p class="lead c">A full lifestyle history, then a specific, sequenced protocol the patient can actually run on a working weekday. Sequenced matters: patients given six changes at once reliably do none.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pillgrid">
      <div class="pillcard reveal"><h4>Nutrition</h4><p>Composition, portion, and above all timing &mdash; built around what's actually cooked in their kitchen, not an imported plan.</p></div>
      <div class="pillcard reveal" data-d="1"><h4>Sleep</h4><p>Duration, consistency and what's breaking it. Usually the first domino, given its effect on glycaemic control and appetite regulation.</p></div>
      <div class="pillcard reveal" data-d="2"><h4>Movement</h4><p>Dosed to current capacity and comorbidity. Breaking up sedentary time and post-meal walking, before any talk of a gym.</p></div>
      <div class="pillcard reveal" data-d="3"><h4>Gut health</h4><p>Symptom pattern, meal spacing, fibre and tolerance &mdash; introduced at a pace the patient can sustain.</p></div>
      <div class="pillcard reveal" data-d="4"><h4>Emotional health</h4><p>The stress load that quietly undoes the other four. Practical, daily, and referred onward the moment it needs a professional.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SCOPE — the trust section -->
<section class="fd-section" id="scope">
  <div class="wrap narrow center">
    <div class="kicker c">Scope</div>
    <h2 class="h2">The boundaries matter more <em>than the offer.</em></h2>
    <p class="lead c">You're being asked to put your name near someone else's work. So here is exactly where mine stops &mdash; in writing, before you ask.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="ba">
      <div class="ba-col after reveal">
        <span class="ba-tag">What I do</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Take a full lifestyle history across the five pillars</li>
          <li>Build a specific, sequenced daily protocol</li>
          <li>Check in regularly and adjust when it isn't working</li>
          <li>Send you an intake summary and periodic progress notes</li>
          <li>Escalate anything clinical straight back to you</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="ba-col before reveal" data-d="1">
        <span class="ba-tag">What I never do</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Advise on, adjust or comment on any medication</li>
          <li>Diagnose, or offer the patient a second opinion on yours</li>
          <li>Order or interpret investigations</li>
          <li>Suggest a patient delay, reduce or decline treatment</li>
          <li>Sell supplements, detoxes or protocols of my own devising</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="punch reveal">If a patient asks me a clinical question,<br>the answer is always &ldquo;ask your doctor.&rdquo;</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHAT YOU GET BACK -->
<section class="fd-section" id="back">
  <div class="wrap narrow center">
    <div class="kicker c">What comes back to you</div>
    <h2 class="h2">You keep clinical ownership &mdash; <em>and you stay informed.</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="bgrid three">
      <div class="bcard reveal"><h4>An intake summary</h4><p>What your patient actually eats and when, how they really sleep, what they move, their stress load &mdash; written up properly. Often more candid than what's said in a consulting room.</p></div>
      <div class="bcard reveal" data-d="1"><h4>Periodic progress notes</h4><p>What's been changed, what's holding, what isn't. Timed so you have it before their next review rather than after.</p></div>
      <div class="bcard reveal" data-d="2"><h4>Immediate escalation</h4><p>Red flags, new symptoms or anything outside my scope come back to you the same day. You'll hear it from me before you hear it from them.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="plainnote reveal"><strong>Plainly:</strong> these come by email, written by me. There is no portal, no login and nothing for your staff to learn &mdash; and I'd rather say that than dress up a document as a platform. If a doctor-facing view is ever worth building, it'll be because referring doctors asked for it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
<section class="fd-section" id="how">
  <div class="wrap narrow center">
    <div class="kicker c">How a referral works</div>
    <h2 class="h2">Three steps, <em>and no admin for your practice.</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="steps three">
      <div class="step reveal">
        <div class="step-n">STEP 01</div>
        <h4>You mention it, or pass on a number</h4>
        <p>No forms, no referral letter, no portal. Telling the patient to get in touch is enough &mdash; though anything you want me to know is welcome.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step reveal" data-d="1">
        <div class="step-n">STEP 02</div>
        <h4>I screen them on a free call</h4>
        <p>Thirty minutes. If lifestyle work isn't what they need, or something needs you first, I tell them so and send them back. I'd rather decline a referral than mishandle one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step reveal" data-d="2">
        <div class="step-n">STEP 03</div>
        <h4>I coach; you stay in the loop</h4>
        <p>They work with me on the five pillars. You get the intake summary and progress notes, and every clinical decision stays entirely yours.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HONEST NOTE -->
<section class="fd-section" id="who">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="kicker">Before you refer anyone</div>
    <h2 class="h2">You should know who you'd be referring to.</h2>
    <p class="lead">I'm Akash Malviya. <strong>I'm not a doctor and I hold no medical degree</strong> &mdash; you'd have found that out eventually, so you should have it from me first. What I have is nine years of study in metabolic and lifestyle health, a method I've thought hard about, and a practice that is deliberately still small.</p>
    <p class="lead">Being early is the honest pitch here. I'm working with a small first group of patients, which means each one gets considerably more of my attention than they would from an established practice &mdash; and it means I have every reason to handle your referral carefully. My scope discipline above isn't marketing. It's the only basis on which a coach without a medical degree should be anywhere near your patients.</p>
    <p class="lead">The fastest way to judge whether this is any good: <strong>refer one patient and watch what comes back.</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="fd-section fd-cta" id="partner">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-card reveal">
      <div class="kicker c light">A small beginning</div>
      <h2 class="h2 light">Start with one patient.</h2>
      <p class="lead c light">The one you've had the same conversation with three reviews running. Send them my way and see what comes back before you send a second.</p>
      <div class="rule c"></div>
      <a href={WA} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary btn-onlight">Talk to me about referrals &rarr;</a>
      <p class="soft">Or email <a href="mailto:hello@sankalphealth.in?subject=Referral%20partnership%20%E2%80%94%20Sankalp">hello@sankalphealth.in</a> &mdash; happy to answer questions before you refer anyone.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</PageLayout>

<style>
  .wrap { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  .narrow { max-width: 720px; }
  .center { text-align: center; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }

  .fd-section { padding: clamp(64px, 9vw, 104px) 0; }
  .fd-section:nth-of-type(even) { background: var(--bg-soft); }

  .kicker {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    color: var(--green);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .kicker.c { justify-content: center; }
  .kicker::before, .kicker.c::after { content: ''; width: 24px; height: 1px; background: var(--green); opacity: .45; }
  .kicker.light { color: rgba(255,255,255,.85); }
  .kicker.light::before, .kicker.light::after { background: rgba(255,255,255,.5); }

  .h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 5.4vw, 52px); letter-spacing: -0.5px; line-height: 1.16; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .h1 em, .h2 em { font-style: normal; color: var(--green); }
  .h2 { font-size: clamp(26px, 3.8vw, 40px); line-height: 1.22; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .h2.light { color: #fff; }
  .h2.light em { color: var(--gold-soft); }

  .lead { font-size: clamp(16.5px, 1.9vw, 19px); color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; max-width: 640px; }
  .lead.c { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .lead.light { color: rgba(255,255,255,.82); }
  .lead strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  #who .lead { margin-bottom: 18px; }

  .rule { width: 44px; height: 2px; background: var(--gold); border-radius: 2px; margin: 24px 0; }
  .rule.c { margin: 24px auto; }

  /* HERO */
  .fd-hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 76px 24px 80px;
    text-align: center;
    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 90% at 100% -10%, rgba(217,184,119,.14), transparent 55%),
      radial-gradient(100% 80% at -8% 108%, rgba(21,122,91,.10), transparent 58%),
      linear-gradient(180deg,#ffffff 0%,#fbfdfc 60%,#f4f7f5 100%);
  }
  .fd-hero-fx {
    position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 0; pointer-events: none;
    background-image: radial-gradient(rgba(21,122,91,.06) 1px, transparent 1.5px);
    background-size: 26px 26px;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(120% 100% at 50% 0%, #000 30%, transparent 76%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(120% 100% at 50% 0%, #000 30%, transparent 76%);
  }
  .fd-hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .hero-ctas { display: flex; gap: 14px; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 8px; }

  .gapstrip {
    margin: 50px auto 0; max-width: 660px;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto; align-items: center; gap: 18px;
  }
  .gap-end { text-align: center; }
  .gap-num { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; color: var(--ink); font-size: clamp(19px, 3vw, 26px); font-weight: 600; }
  .gap-lbl { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--green); margin-top: 6px; }
  /* Label sits in normal flow above the rule rather than absolutely positioned,
     so long copy wraps instead of colliding with the two end labels. */
  .gap-mid { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 9px; }
  .gap-mid span {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.45; text-align: center; max-width: 320px;
  }
  .gap-mid::after {
    content: ''; display: block; width: 100%; height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--line), var(--accent), var(--line));
  }

  /* PROBLEM CHAIN */
  .chain { max-width: 720px; margin: 44px auto 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .chain-step { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 22px; padding: 18px 0; }
  .chain-dot { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }
  .chain-num {
    width: 40px; height: 40px; flex-shrink: 0; border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--line); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; color: var(--green); font-size: 15px; background: var(--green-soft);
  }
  .chain-line { width: 1px; flex: 1; background: var(--line); margin-top: 8px; min-height: 22px; }
  .chain-step:last-child .chain-line { display: none; }
  .chain-step h4 { font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .chain-step p { font-size: 16px; color: var(--muted); }
  .chain-step.fail .chain-num { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); }
  .chain-step.fail h4 { color: var(--accent); }
  .punch { text-align: center; margin-top: 44px; font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-style: italic; font-size: clamp(19px, 2.8vw, 25px); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.5; }

  /* FIVE PILLARS */
  .pillgrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5,1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 48px; }
  .pillcard {
    background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-top: 3px solid var(--green);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .pillcard h4 { font-size: 16.5px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .pillcard p { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }

  /* SOLUTION STEPS */
  .steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4,1fr); gap: 20px; margin-top: 48px; }
  .steps.three { grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); }
  .step {
    background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 28px 22px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); transition: transform .3s var(--ease), box-shadow .3s;
  }
  .step:hover { transform: translateY(-4px); box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg); }
  .step-n { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--green); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .step h4 { font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .step p { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }

  /* DO / DON'T */
  .ba { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 22px; margin-top: 48px; }
  .ba-col { border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 30px 28px; }
  .ba-col.before { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .ba-col.after { background: var(--green-soft); border: 1px solid #bfe3d3; }
  .ba-tag { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 20px; display: inline-block; }
  .ba-col.before .ba-tag { color: var(--accent); }
  .ba-col.after .ba-tag { color: var(--green); }
  .ba-col ul { list-style: none; }
  .ba-col li { font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px 0 12px 30px; position: relative; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .ba-col li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .ba-col.before li { color: var(--text); }
  .ba-col.before li::before { content: '\2715'; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; }
  .ba-col.after li { color: var(--text); }
  .ba-col.after li::before { content: '\2713'; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 12px; color: var(--green); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; }

  /* BENEFITS */
  .bgrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); gap: 20px; margin-top: 48px; }
  .bcard {
    background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 30px 26px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); transition: transform .3s var(--ease), box-shadow .3s;
  }
  .bcard:hover { transform: translateY(-4px); box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg); }
  .bcard h4 { font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .bcard p { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  .plainnote {
    max-width: 720px; margin: 32px auto 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7;
    background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 20px 24px;
  }
  .plainnote strong { color: var(--ink); }

  /* CTA */
  .fd-cta { text-align: center; }
  .cta-card {
    max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 24px; padding: clamp(44px, 7vw, 72px) 32px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--green), var(--green-dark)); color: #fff;
  }
  .cta-card .btn-onlight { background: #fff; color: var(--green-dark); box-shadow: 0 4px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.18); }
  .cta-card .btn-onlight:hover { background: var(--green-soft); }
  .cta-card .soft { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-style: italic; color: rgba(255,255,255,.75); font-size: 14.5px; margin-top: 20px; }
  .cta-card .soft a { color: #fff; font-weight: 600; }

  /* REVEAL ON SCROLL */
  .reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(26px); transition: opacity .8s var(--ease), transform .8s var(--ease); }
  .reveal.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .reveal[data-d="1"] { transition-delay: .08s; }
  .reveal[data-d="2"] { transition-delay: .16s; }
  .reveal[data-d="3"] { transition-delay: .24s; }
  .reveal[data-d="4"] { transition-delay: .32s; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .reveal { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; } }

  /* SCROLL PROGRESS BAR */
  .scroll-bar { position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; height: 2px; width: 0; z-index: 300; background: var(--green); }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .steps, .steps.three { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); }
    .bgrid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); }
    .pillgrid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .ba { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .steps, .steps.three { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .bgrid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .pillgrid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); }
    .gapstrip { gap: 12px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .pillgrid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .gapstrip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 10px; max-width: 300px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
    .gap-mid { padding: 4px 0; }
    .gap-mid::after { display: none; }
    .gap-mid span { font-size: 14px; max-width: 260px; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  (function () {
    var bar = document.getElementById('scrollBar');
    function onScroll() {
      var y = window.scrollY;
      var h = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
      if (bar) bar.style.width = (h > 0 ? (y / h * 100) : 0) + '%';
    }
    window.addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });
    onScroll();

    var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      entries.forEach(function (en) {
        if (en.isIntersecting) { en.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(en.target); }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.14, rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px' });
    document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(function (el) { io.observe(el); });
  })();
</script>
